Discussion: OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353

From our per-feature patches `44-jewellery-teleports`, `45-jewellery-charge-slot` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), applied with `git am` on `main` (`1be5dfb5f`); commits kept as they are except for the `feat:`/`fix:` subject.

**Problem.** Teleport jewellery did nothing.

**Change.** New module `content/travel/jewellery-teleports` + pack, for the games necklace, ring of dueling, amulet of glory, skills necklace and combat bracelet:
- Rub opens the teleport menu (interface 187 via script 217, with hotkeys, as RuneLite's Better Teleport Menu expects); worn destination ops teleport directly.
- Each use takes a charge with the OSRS messages ("Your games necklace has seven uses left.", "...crumbles to dust."); glory, skills necklace and combat bracelet keep an uncharged item.
- A charge swap replaces the item in place (45), so a worn necklace stays in the neck slot.
- Destinations in dbtables `jewellery_teleport_items/dests` (60020-60021).

**Tests.** `JewelleryTeleportScriptTest` (integration). The charge-slot fix (45) was seen on a client first (a worn games necklace moved to the head slot).

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`; `assemble`, `test` and `integration` as separate runs in a 4 GB container): cache build pass, `spotlessCheck` pass, `assemble test integration` pass, boot: Server ready in 7.172812007s.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; in-game checks mentioned above were on our own server build (main's pin `9a8b338a8` plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** Wiki-derived data or text (OSRS Wiki, by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/; OpenRune is ISC): destinations and their tiles, menu order and the charge messages (Games necklace, Ring of dueling, Amulet of glory, Skills necklace, Combat bracelet pages). See question 4 in #353 on how upstream wants to handle that.

**Caveats.**
- Best guesses: the menu title, glory/skills/combat charge lines, the purple value, timing, and two planes (Corporeal Beast, Tears of Guthix).
- No destination requirements or landing radius.

**Release note.** Teleport jewellery works: Rub menu, worn ops and charges.

